    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1980-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The condition gives \\[ \\frac{2x-y}{x+y}=\\frac23. \\] Thus \\(6x-3y=2x+2y,\\) so \\(4x=5y\\) and \\(\\frac{x}{y}=\\frac{5}{4}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Write the stated ratio as an equation of two fractions",
        "Cross-multiply and collect the \\(x\\)-terms and \\(y\\)-terms separately"
      ],
